1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,100
You probably don’t want to do that.

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:04,100
Ask AI to write more tests?

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,167
In a large legacy project,

4
00:00:06,167 --> 00:00:09,700
where maintenance problems arrive faster than your team can solve them,

5
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,633
that can mean more code to understand, run, and maintain.

6
00:00:13,633 --> 00:00:17,900
Useful, targeted tests can make fixes safer—even now.

7
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,700
But generating a pile can add to your overload.

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:24,600
Reliable test automation requires high-level software engineering.

9
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,133
Start with an isolated, repeatable test environment.

10
00:00:28,133 --> 00:00:29,800
Learn the checks yourself.

11
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:32,767
Then let AI perform hands-on testing.

12
00:00:32,767 --> 00:00:38,167
Investigate its findings and fix confirmed problems—without generating a maintained suite.

13
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:42,700
As you regain control, automate the workflows that repeatedly prove useful.

14
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:46,267
Then improve the suite: make feedback faster,

15
00:00:46,267 --> 00:00:47,567
delete redundant tests,

16
00:00:47,567 --> 00:00:51,667
and move suitable local checks from expensive end-to-end tests into unit tests.

17
00:00:51,667 --> 00:00:54,633
Keep the wider protection you still need.

18
00:00:54,633 --> 00:01:00,867
Spend your spare AI capacity on better protection, with less to maintain.
